%%abcts shapes neither corpus writes, swept through both engines one at a time. Two of
%%abcts these are rules; four are open rows, measured through abcjs 6.7.0 and NOT built:
%%abcts   X:4  !trill!z4     BUILT. A rest takes its decorations like any element, after
%%abcts                      its own glyph. Still open: a MULTIMEASURE rest, which draws
%%abcts                      no rest glyph — `!fermata!Z2 C4|` is 157.4125 in abcjs
%%abcts                      against our 144.186, and hoisting the call out of the glyph
%%abcts                      branch to reach it took three other rungs off exact.
%%abcts   X:5  {g}z2         the automatic grace slur is BUILT — abcjs's `notehead` for a
%%abcts                      rest is the REST'S OWN GLYPH (instrumented: `gracePitch 11
%%abcts                      notePitch 7`), and our y matches to the digit. What is left
%%abcts                      is its ROOM: abcjs moves the whole element 10px per grace
%%abcts                      (bar 143.9 against a bare `z2`'s 133.9, `{gg}z2` 153.9) and
%%abcts                      an INVISIBLE rest takes none (`{g}x2` 133.9). Three places
%%abcts                      were tried — the rod, the x before placing, the left ink —
%%abcts                      and each moved nothing, because the line solve replaces the
%%abcts                      element's own x. Instrument what it reads; do not guess a
%%abcts                      fourth time.
%%abcts        ⚠️ AND abcjs ITSELF WRITES `M NaN` for the grace flag on `{g}x2` — a bug of
%%abcts        its own, and the one row here we could only reproduce by reproducing a NaN.
%%abcts   X:6  [K:G] mid-bar our group is `staff-extra key-signature`; abcjs's is a
%%abcts                      `note` with `selectable="false" data-index="0"`.
%%abcts   X:7  [M:2/4] mid-bar a stem runs 77.51 where abcjs's runs 85.23.
X:1
T:a decoration on a barline, drawn after the barline's own rule
L:1/8
K:C
!fermata!|CDEF|

X:2
T:a tie into a rest, which never closes and runs off the line
L:1/8
K:C
C-z C|

X:3
T:the same tie with no rest, which does close
L:1/8
K:C
C-C C|

X:4
T:a decoration on a rest
L:1/8
K:C
!trill!z4 C4|

X:5
T:a grace group on a rest
L:1/8
K:C
{g}z2 C2|

X:6
T:an inline key change mid-measure
L:1/8
K:C
CD[K:G]EF|

X:7
T:an inline meter change mid-measure
L:1/8
K:C
CD[M:2/4]EF|

X:8
T:a decoration on a barline that opens a measure
L:1/8
K:C
CDEF|!fermata!|GABc|
